<title>GERMANY: Tchibo to raise coffee price by 1.40 DM on June 26.</title>
<headline>Tchibo to raise coffee price by 1.40 DM on June 26.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's second largest coffee roaster, Tchibo Frisch-Roest-Kaffee GmbH, said on Thursday it would raise its retail coffee prices on June 26 due to high raw coffee prices and the strong dollar.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it would increase its end-user prices by an average of 1.40 marks per kilo.</p>
<p>Tchibo added that price premiums for high-quality coffees popular in Germany made the increase necessary. Tchibo last upped its retail prices in early May.</p>
</text>
